:R-HSA-901042  a            obo:GO_0008150 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "The unfolded protein is recognized by a chaperon protein (calnexin or calreticulin) and the folding process starts. The binding of these protein requires a mono-glucosylated glycan (Caramelo JJ and Parodi AJ, 2008), but in certain cases can occur even in the absence of glycosylation (Ireland BS et al, 2008)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Calnexin/calreticulin cycle" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Dall'Olio, GM, 2009-11-10" , "Reviewed: Gagneux, P, 2010-08-17" , "Edited: Jassal, B, 2010-07-02" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
